# This is a TEMPLATE — variable names with empty values, no real secrets.
# Copy to ./.env and fill in. ./.env is gitignored and never committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#   paramify doctor manifest.yaml      # reports which of these are still missing
#
# This file is for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT. The framework reads ${env:VAR} from its own
# environment; .env is one source among many, and a real environment variable
# always wins over a value set here — so `export FOO=bar` overrides this file.
#
# For containers use deploy/.env.example instead: compose's env_file injects those
# as real environment variables at run time (see deploy/README.md). This file is
# read by the `paramify` entry point only.
#
# To see the EXACT variables a fetcher needs:
#   paramify describe <fetcher>
#   paramify doctor <manifest>

# ---- Paramify (the framework's own credential) --------------------------------
# One token for everything that talks to Paramify: uploading evidence, syncing
# scripts, `paramify programs`, and the Paramify VER fetchers. Needs read and
# write scope on the workspace.
PARAMIFY_API_TOKEN=
# Deprecated alias, still honored if you already have it set somewhere:
# PARAMIFY_UPLOAD_API_TOKEN=
# Optional; defaults to https://app.paramify.com/api/v0 (https required, except
# localhost). Point this at a stage instance to test against one.
# PARAMIFY_API_BASE_URL=https://your-instance.paramify.com/api/v0

# ---- Per-platform credentials (uncomment what your manifests actually use) ----
# Names below are illustrative — confirm each with `paramify describe <fetcher>`,
# and see fetchers/<category>/README.md for how to create each credential.
# Okta
# OKTA_ORG_URL=
# OKTA_API_TOKEN=
# KnowBe4
# KNOWBE4_API_KEY=
# KNOWBE4_REGION=us
# GitLab — GITLAB_API_TOKEN is the declared default; a fanout manifest names its
# own per-target vars instead (GITLAB_TOKEN_1, _2, … — see examples/minimal_run.yaml)
# GITLAB_API_TOKEN=
# Datadog
# DATADOG_API_KEY=
# DATADOG_APP_KEY=
# AWS — prefer a local profile / SSO over static keys; passthrough is wired in
# fetchers/_categories/aws.yaml. If you must use static keys:
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
